erse was dictated but not signed."" (Christopher Morley) http://xent.com/mailman/listinfo/fork",0,20030228_easy_ham_2.tar.bz2,easy_ham_2/00946.6d3c3492c0310d58e7eccadf18fbd9de,fc0cecd51b1c3f45a97057b2c90b383997dcdae67b4e58d579138436d46c885c
[Razor-users] Re: keep submitting known spam?,"On 08/08/02 15:26 -0700, Chip Paswater wrote: ) > ) > Well, a little more than one bit -- you have to transmit the ) > signature, plus now the entire message body. Plus your ID. ) > Plus the rights to all intellectual property contained in any ) > email message you submit (I guess technically there are no bits ) > in the rights assignment) ) ) Perhaps a feature can be added to razor-report, so that it checks whether a ) message is spam before it submits it. If it is spam, then don't send the ) body, 4 signatures, etc, just up the ""rating"" for that individual spam. razor-report only sends the body if the server does not have a copy already. When it does, and the server just notes who also thinks that mail is spam, and uses that info in TeS. -chad ------------------------------------------------------- This sf.net email is sponsored by: Dice - The leading online job board for high-tech professionals. Search and apply for tech jobs today! http://seeker.dice.com/seeker.epl?rel_code=31 _______________________________________________ Razor-users mailing list Razor-users@lists.sourceforge.net https://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/razor-users","[Razor-users] Re: keep submitting known spam? On 08/08/02 15:26 -0700, Chip Paswater wrote: ) > ) > Well, a little more than one bit -- you have to transmit the ) > signature, plus now the entire message body. Plus your ID. ) > Plus the rights to all intellectual property contained in any ) > email message you submit (I guess technically there are no bits ) > in the rights assignment) ) ) Perhaps a feature can be added to razor-report, so that it checks whether a ) message is spam before it submits it. If it is spam, then don't send the ) body, 4 signatures, etc, just up the ""rating"" for that individual spam. razor-report only sends the body if the server does not have a copy already. When it does, and the server just notes who also thinks that mail is spam, and uses that info in TeS. -chad ------------------------------------------------------- This sf.net email is sponsored by: Dice - The leading online job board for high-tech professionals. Search and apply for tech jobs today! http://seeker.dice.com/seeker.epl?rel_code=31 _______________________________________________ Razor-users mailing list Razor-users@lists.sourceforge.net https://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/razor-users",0,20030228_easy_ham_2.tar.bz2,easy_ham_2/00620.f515234db3aec0db283f64aabaa046ac,6f8f52957185b57b4c978f95887144fecd38a4dd9137644da2d2bf1a18dad789
