Re: It's a small world,"On Thu, Aug 15, 2002 at 05:46:55PM -0400, Luis Villa wrote: > FWIW, slummerville actually has the internet- not just broadband, but > actual broadband competition, which I gather is rare. I had ADSL and two > cable options when I moved in. Did you actually attempt to order the DSL? Large chunks of somerville have advertised DSL service that can't actually be obtained. Excuses vary, from ""no available copper"" to ""full DSLAM"", but the folks I know who've wanted DSL around here have all failed, ending up either with ATTBB, RCN or an honest-to-god T1. -j > > Luis > -- jesse reed vincent -- root@eruditorum.org -- jesse@fsck.com 70EBAC90: 2A07 FC22 7DB4 42C1 9D71 0108 41A3 3FB3 70EB AC90 This is scary. I'm imagining tracerouting you and seeing links like ""Route 84"" and ""Route 9, Exit 14"". Obviously, this is illness induced. --Cana McCoy http://xent.com/mailman/listinfo/fork","Re: It's a small world On Thu, Aug 15, 2002 at 05:46:55PM -0400, Luis Villa wrote: > FWIW, slummerville actually has the internet- not just broadband, but > actual broadband competition, which I gather is rare. I had ADSL and two > cable options when I moved in. Did you actually attempt to order the DSL? Large chunks of somerville have advertised DSL service that can't actually be obtained. Excuses vary, from ""no available copper"" to ""full DSLAM"", but the folks I know who've wanted DSL around here have all failed, ending up either with ATTBB, RCN or an honest-to-god T1. -j > > Luis > -- jesse reed vincent -- root@eruditorum.org -- jesse@fsck.com 70EBAC90: 2A07 FC22 7DB4 42C1 9D71 0108 41A3 3FB3 70EB AC90 This is scary. I'm imagining tracerouting you and seeing links like ""Route 84"" and ""Route 9, Exit 14"". Obviously, this is illness induced. --Cana McCoy http://xent.com/mailman/listinfo/fork",0,20030228_easy_ham_2.tar.bz2,easy_ham_2/01036.650d6fe868554ee430f472b487904f65,500505ef9e0781a4989a11346e91b0026f1bf54bd373658486cc1586ea0e6496
