Re: Sorting,">>>>> On Mon, 9 Sep 2002, ""Rick"" == Rick Baartman wrote: Rick> This is dangerous; I have to remember to re-scan each Rick> folder I enter. Is there a safeguard for this? Nope. Regenerate the cache in the script for f in `folders -fast -r` do echo sorting $f ... sortm +$f scan `mhpath +`/$f/.xmhcache done --Hal _______________________________________________ Exmh-users mailing list Exmh-users@redhat.com https://listman.redhat.com/mailman/listinfo/exmh-users","Re: Sorting >>>>> On Mon, 9 Sep 2002, ""Rick"" == Rick Baartman wrote: Rick> This is dangerous; I have to remember to re-scan each Rick> folder I enter. Is there a safeguard for this? Nope. Regenerate the cache in the script for f in `folders -fast -r` do echo sorting $f ... sortm +$f scan `mhpath +`/$f/.xmhcache done --Hal _______________________________________________ Exmh-users mailing list Exmh-users@redhat.com https://listman.redhat.com/mailman/listinfo/exmh-users",0,20030228_easy_ham.tar.bz2,easy_ham/00985.e20b9f4f171d907fb8d8439584fe03b1,72a5151528ccf233e01ec70a8874b7790bb35bb191985628ffc29f9c179681e2
