Re: Ximian apt repos?,"On Wed, 2002-07-24 at 03:50, Angles Puglisi wrote: > Lance (lance_tt@bellsouth.net) wrote*: > > > >well, from the looks of things, Evolution mail client isn't supported > >just yet, so I reckon I'll wait a bit. Whoever posted these gnome2 apt > >repositories, thanks!!! > > > > I'm uising Havoc Pennington's Gnomehide and it rocks. I installed it before I > knew about apt, but one of the previous emails had an apt repository that > claimed to have gnomehide. Just remember there is one kew file that makes the > difference between Gnome1 and Gnome2 being used. I *think* it is ""gnome-core"" > vs. ""gnome-session"" but I can not remember. > > Note that that those same files are probably in the Limbo beta, except > updated. There has not been a major change to ""gnomehide"" in a while, I > suspect Havoc's work went into Limbo then. Right, gnomehide is only updated when it's been a while since the last red hat release, and the next beta isn't out yet. Since the beta is out now, gnomehide won't be updated again for a while. Julian _______________________________________________ RPM-List mailing list <RPM-List@freshrpms.net> http://lists.freshrpms.net/mailman/listinfo/rpm-list","Re: Ximian apt repos? On Wed, 2002-07-24 at 03:50, Angles Puglisi wrote: > Lance (lance_tt@bellsouth.net) wrote*: > > > >well, from the looks of things, Evolution mail client isn't supported > >just yet, so I reckon I'll wait a bit. Whoever posted these gnome2 apt > >repositories, thanks!!! > > > > I'm uising Havoc Pennington's Gnomehide and it rocks. I installed it before I > knew about apt, but one of the previous emails had an apt repository that > claimed to have gnomehide. Just remember there is one kew file that makes the > difference between Gnome1 and Gnome2 being used. I *think* it is ""gnome-core"" > vs. ""gnome-session"" but I can not remember. > > Note that that those same files are probably in the Limbo beta, except > updated. There has not been a major change to ""gnomehide"" in a while, I > suspect Havoc's work went into Limbo then. Right, gnomehide is only updated when it's been a while since the last red hat release, and the next beta isn't out yet. Since the beta is out now, gnomehide won't be updated again for a while. Julian _______________________________________________ RPM-List mailing list <RPM-List@freshrpms.net> http://lists.freshrpms.net/mailman/listinfo/rpm-list",0,20030228_easy_ham_2.tar.bz2,easy_ham_2/01159.2815cb2878b393aa1735e1f0bbc2c888,d032d9336706adbfb4087d1e97925eda1927bfb5c982ce7b94561e9a60b7591e
