Re: Apt problems,"Once upon a time, Peter wrote : > On Wed, Feb 06, 2002 at 04:14:27PM +0100, Matthias Saou wrote: > > Strange... all my openssh packages don't explicitly requires a version > > of openssl. What version of openssh do you have? Is it an official Red > > Hat package? I suppose it isn't, and using Red Hat's rpms will solve > > your problem. > > openssh-3.0.2p1-1 > > I think that is directly from openssh site. It's from the RH 6.2 that I > upgraded to 7.2 (6.2 doesn't ship with openssh...). That explains... > I probably should downgrade to the versoin RH provides except I can't do > that as I don't have physical access to that box and downgrading ssh > packages over ssh doesn't sound like a bright idea... Well, with 7.0, I've seen a few problems with doing that, but as of 7.2 it's really wonderful! Ever tried of completely uninstalling all openssh related packages while being connected through ssh? Well, it works!!!! Of course, if the connection cuts at that moment, you're stuck, but a simple upgrade with official Red Hat packages also works like a charm :-) Matthias -- Matthias Saou World Trade Center ------------- Edificio Norte 4 Planta System and Network Engineer 08039 Barcelona, Spain Electronic Group Interactive Phone : +34 936 00 23 23 _______________________________________________ RPM-List mailing list <RPM-List@freshrpms.net> http://lists.freshrpms.net/mailman/listinfo/rpm-list","Re: Apt problems Once upon a time, Peter wrote : > On Wed, Feb 06, 2002 at 04:14:27PM +0100, Matthias Saou wrote: > > Strange... all my openssh packages don't explicitly requires a version > > of openssl. What version of openssh do you have? Is it an official Red > > Hat package? I suppose it isn't, and using Red Hat's rpms will solve > > your problem. > > openssh-3.0.2p1-1 > > I think that is directly from openssh site. It's from the RH 6.2 that I > upgraded to 7.2 (6.2 doesn't ship with openssh...). That explains... > I probably should downgrade to the versoin RH provides except I can't do > that as I don't have physical access to that box and downgrading ssh > packages over ssh doesn't sound like a bright idea... Well, with 7.0, I've seen a few problems with doing that, but as of 7.2 it's really wonderful! Ever tried of completely uninstalling all openssh related packages while being connected through ssh? Well, it works!!!! Of course, if the connection cuts at that moment, you're stuck, but a simple upgrade with official Red Hat packages also works like a charm :-) Matthias -- Matthias Saou World Trade Center ------------- Edificio Norte 4 Planta System and Network Engineer 08039 Barcelona, Spain Electronic Group Interactive Phone : +34 936 00 23 23 _______________________________________________ RPM-List mailing list <RPM-List@freshrpms.net> http://lists.freshrpms.net/mailman/listinfo/rpm-list",0,20030228_easy_ham.tar.bz2,easy_ham/01099.7273b08ddcb69f15239cb516b118be07,f38aa6bfa6704a787e3ff7f28b98a7190c8cd6a79f29e30636dd93fcf5e9cb59
