Re: CD player UI for toddlers,"""Jim Whitehead"" <ejw@cse.ucsc.edu> writes: > The CD player we have combines play and pause in a single button, but > doesn't provide *instantaneous* feedback that the button was pushed, instead > requiring you to wait until the music starts, 5-10 seconds. This is a UI > disaster. Since Tatum doesn't get feedback right away, she presses the > button again, thereby pausing the CD before it even plays. She'll only ever > get music if she presses the button an odd number of times. This happens a > surprising amount of the time, since she eventually hits the button again > when the music doesn't play. Nice to hear that somebody else does this too. -- Karl Anderson kra@monkey.org http://www.monkey.org/~kra/","Re: CD player UI for toddlers ""Jim Whitehead"" <ejw@cse.ucsc.edu> writes: > The CD player we have combines play and pause in a single button, but > doesn't provide *instantaneous* feedback that the button was pushed, instead > requiring you to wait until the music starts, 5-10 seconds. This is a UI > disaster. Since Tatum doesn't get feedback right away, she presses the > button again, thereby pausing the CD before it even plays. She'll only ever > get music if she presses the button an odd number of times. This happens a > surprising amount of the time, since she eventually hits the button again > when the music doesn't play. Nice to hear that somebody else does this too. -- Karl Anderson kra@monkey.org http://www.monkey.org/~kra/",0,20030228_easy_ham.tar.bz2,easy_ham/00437.a1f4bc09ef8406e572438adeb849d31c,f32d32d7939a02a003226528cf11decee65d0b40b69c09f0ccf8929d28021a84
