[Razor-users] Fun Uses of Razored Mail,"I'm taking all my razored mail today and calling any 1-800 numbers I can find. I say ""Hi, I'm calling everyone that spammed me today to raise their cost of doing business. You have a great day!"" I'm told I should do it from a pay phone, so it costs them 50 cents per call. If more people did this, we could tie up their phone lines and cost them so much money they could never make spam work. Also fun is the simple ""Die Spammer Die!"" Fox ------------------------------------------------------- This sf.net email is sponsored by:ThinkGeek Welcome to geek heaven. http://thinkgeek.com/sf _______________________________________________ Razor-users mailing list Razor-users@lists.sourceforge.net https://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/razor-users","[Razor-users] Fun Uses of Razored Mail I'm taking all my razored mail today and calling any 1-800 numbers I can find. I say ""Hi, I'm calling everyone that spammed me today to raise their cost of doing business. You have a great day!"" I'm told I should do it from a pay phone, so it costs them 50 cents per call. If more people did this, we could tie up their phone lines and cost them so much money they could never make spam work. Also fun is the simple ""Die Spammer Die!"" Fox ------------------------------------------------------- This sf.net email is sponsored by:ThinkGeek Welcome to geek heaven. http://thinkgeek.com/sf _______________________________________________ Razor-users mailing list Razor-users@lists.sourceforge.net https://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/razor-users",0,20030228_easy_ham.tar.bz2,easy_ham/01586.9f27ed39ecac8ed15e18dc166e930005,c7eb4e205ebc2384c8b4cec4b1df032f80df1a6373684ab2241729a0655017f0
Re: [zzzzteana] Moon over ocean,"David asked: > My wife noticed something odd. The nearly-full moon was about 30 > degrees above the horizon. There was a notable glow on the horizon, > except under the moon. The moon seemed to be in a column of darkness > that was about three times the apparent width of the moon. We could see > the column over its entire length as a strip of sky darker than the sky > around it. > > Any of you ever see this? Do you have any idea what could have caused > it? I suspect it's due to some pecularity of the visual system, but > have no clear idea. I'm surprised to not find this phenomenon in Corlis. I could have sworn I saw it there. He does have the somewhat similar dark sky between a rainbow and a secondary bow. I personally have seen a rainbow enclosing a semi-circle of darker sky. I know I've read about pillars under the Sun and Moon elsewhere, but I can't recall if they were reportedly dark or bright. I do know these sorts of things are supposed to be quirks of optics not of the visual system. I'm sorry I haven't got any answers, but a search through some books on atmospheric optics ought to turn a few hints up. Bill William Jacobs Freelance Unemployed Person ------------------------ Yahoo! Groups Sponsor ---------------------~--> 4 DVDs Free +s&p Join Now http://us.click.yahoo.com/pt6YBB/NXiEAA/MVfIAA/7gSolB/TM ---------------------------------------------------------------------~-> To unsubscribe from this group, send an email to: forteana-unsubscribe@egroups.com Your use of Yahoo! Groups is subject to http://docs.yahoo.com/info/terms/","Re: [zzzzteana] Moon over ocean David asked: > My wife noticed something odd. The nearly-full moon was about 30 > degrees above the horizon. There was a notable glow on the horizon, > except under the moon. The moon seemed to be in a column of darkness > that was about three times the apparent width of the moon. We could see > the column over its entire length as a strip of sky darker than the sky > around it. > > Any of you ever see this? Do you have any idea what could have caused > it? I suspect it's due to some pecularity of the visual system, but > have no clear idea. I'm surprised to not find this phenomenon in Corlis. I could have sworn I saw it there. He does have the somewhat similar dark sky between a rainbow and a secondary bow. I personally have seen a rainbow enclosing a semi-circle of darker sky. I know I've read about pillars under the Sun and Moon elsewhere, but I can't recall if they were reportedly dark or bright. I do know these sorts of things are supposed to be quirks of optics not of the visual system. I'm sorry I haven't got any answers, but a search through some books on atmospheric optics ought to turn a few hints up. Bill William Jacobs Freelance Unemployed Person ------------------------ Yahoo! Groups Sponsor ---------------------~--> 4 DVDs Free +s&p Join Now http://us.click.yahoo.com/pt6YBB/NXiEAA/MVfIAA/7gSolB/TM ---------------------------------------------------------------------~-> To unsubscribe from this group, send an email to: forteana-unsubscribe@egroups.com Your use of Yahoo! Groups is subject to http://docs.yahoo.com/info/terms/",0,20030228_easy_ham.tar.bz2,easy_ham/00172.de357389925b5094f2e7ff3d1c20deb9,e0b249194ff1fcc8879379b638f7889fe8c8f1d46530dedc2c31c39f66d79037
Re: Asteroids anyone ?,">>>>> ""G"" == Gordon Mohr <gojomo@usa.net> writes: G> Gary Lawrence Murphy writes: >> 20,000 years ago, one of them the size of Mt Everest just ever >> so slightly grazed us and left a scar 400km long in the side of >> South America G> Do you have any further information about this incident that G> would me find more details on the web? Good question. This was covered in one of the amateur rags, maybe Sky and Telescope or even Scienterrific American, long before there was any web to speak of, but you'd think a 400km gash in the Earth would be pretty easy to find ;) I remember it from an issue perhaps in the very late 80's or early 90's. It's interesting to note that NT7 and many other NEO bodies are all on trajectories that approach the Earth from under the ecliptic, so with the Earth tilt, South America becomes a pretty good target. In trying to find you a site through Google, I turned up several different impact sites in Venezuela and Brazil, with ages ranging from 251M to 70 years, but not the 400km gash from the above story. The only google refs I found from that period is one in Arizona (famous impact crater) and another in NM; do wish I had noted the actual South American /country/ that contains the scar; Venezuela sticks in my mind but I can't be certain. http://neo.jpl.nasa.gov/images/meteorcrater.html -- Gary Lawrence Murphy <garym@teledyn.com> TeleDynamics Communications Inc Business Innovations Through Open Source Systems: http://www.teledyn.com ""Computers are useless. They can only give you answers.""(Pablo Picasso) http://xent.com/mailman/listinfo/fork","Re: Asteroids anyone ? >>>>> ""G"" == Gordon Mohr <gojomo@usa.net> writes: G> Gary Lawrence Murphy writes: >> 20,000 years ago, one of them the size of Mt Everest just ever >> so slightly grazed us and left a scar 400km long in the side of >> South America G> Do you have any further information about this incident that G> would me find more details on the web? Good question. This was covered in one of the amateur rags, maybe Sky and Telescope or even Scienterrific American, long before there was any web to speak of, but you'd think a 400km gash in the Earth would be pretty easy to find ;) I remember it from an issue perhaps in the very late 80's or early 90's. It's interesting to note that NT7 and many other NEO bodies are all on trajectories that approach the Earth from under the ecliptic, so with the Earth tilt, South America becomes a pretty good target. In trying to find you a site through Google, I turned up several different impact sites in Venezuela and Brazil, with ages ranging from 251M to 70 years, but not the 400km gash from the above story. The only google refs I found from that period is one in Arizona (famous impact crater) and another in NM; do wish I had noted the actual South American /country/ that contains the scar; Venezuela sticks in my mind but I can't be certain. http://neo.jpl.nasa.gov/images/meteorcrater.html -- Gary Lawrence Murphy <garym@teledyn.com> TeleDynamics Communications Inc Business Innovations Through Open Source Systems: http://www.teledyn.com ""Computers are useless. They can only give you answers.""(Pablo Picasso) http://xent.com/mailman/listinfo/fork",0,20030228_easy_ham_2.tar.bz2,easy_ham_2/00902.a538cb6b30f5f3d28ea4261597ffa510,a1a9149375476ff6d4396eb803d3ad4126026bdf5041a7919e3070ca5890e3b6
[MLB-WIRELESS] CONTRALORIA Y GERENCIA ADMINISTRATIVA,"http://www.rebackee.com/cursos2/contraloria.htm Untitled Document Quality Training de México , lo invita al extraordinario seminario que tendrá lugar en VILLAHERMOSA , TABASCO , los días 01 y 02 de AGOSTO de 2002 Este es un seminario sobre los más efectivos conceptos y maneras concretas para mejorar la función de Contraloría y Gerencia Administrativa.....¿ Que medidas debe tomar.... para enfrentar la Falta de Liquidez, Reducción de Ventas, Aumento en los Costos, conflictos Laborales....¿ Cómo anticiparse a un colapso en la empresa ?. ¡¡ NO ESPERE A QUE SEA DEMASIADO TARDE !! Se discutirá ampliamente sobre la situación actual de las empresas en épocas de crisis, ¿que están haciendo para salir adelante?. Así como estrategias contables actuales, pronósticos de presupuestos, modelos ABC y otras alternativas de flujo de información; como controles y cumplimientos, información administrativa, reportes de gasto, crédito y cobranza, análisis financiero y personal. Aspectos claves dentro del programa : - Como organizar su área y hacerla altamente competitiva - Renueve su manera de utilizar los informes financieros - Predictores de Quiebra....Acciones inmediatas a considerar - Casos Históricos ¡¡LA IMPORTANCIA DE CAPACITARSE CON LOS LÍDERES!! Experiencia, Calidad y Éxito... Quality Training de México, le ofrece los más aclamados consultores y seminarios ejecutivos disponibles en el mercado...con los temas de mayor impacto en las empresas... SONY de México, Hewlett Packard, Casa Cuervo, Cervecería Modelo, PEMEX, Mexicana, Molex y más de 4,000 empresas en México y Latinoamérica, conocen nuestros exclusivos programas de capacitación. ¡ Un experto estará con usted en este seminario ! TEMARIO: 1.- El Nuevo Papel del Gerente Administrativo en las Empresas Modernas. - Funciones, responsabilidades y resultados. - Trampas en la Planeación. - El Plan de Contingencia. 2.- La Gerencia Administrativa y el Análisis de Procesos, Políticas y Procedimientos para controlar las operaciones de su empresa. - Conocimiento de la empresa: Base para el análisis de procesos. - Establecimiento de planes de operación. - Análisis de funciones básicas: abastecimientos, producción, ventas, recursos humanos. - Bases para implementar políticas y procedimientos. 3.- Control y Administración de Ingresos, el Crédito y la Cobranza. - Organización del departamento de crédito y su manual de políticas y procedimientos. - Determinación de políticas de apertura y autorización de crédito. - Gestión de Cobranza. - Concentración de fondos, cobranza electrónica y factoraje. 4.- Control de Costos en la Empresa. - Los costos en la administración empresarial. - Reducción de Costos - Alcances - - Presupuestos de costos. - Control de rentabilidad y costos. 5.- Renueve su Manera de Utilizar Informes Financieros. - Problemas en la manera de elaborar informes financieros. - Tipos, usos y elementos en los informes. - Criterios para los informes: importancia, relevancia, prontitud y presentación. 6.- Reportes Financieros para Evaluar la Productividad: - Herramientas de Diagnóstico del resultado financiero. - Valor Económico Agregado (EVA) como herramienta para medir la productividad. - Enlace entre la estrategia global de la empresa y la información financiera y administrativa. - Información para medir y mejorar la competitividad: Ventajas y desventajas competitivas. - Concepto de los GAP’S. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- PROGRAMA: 01 y 02 de AGOSTO de 2002 horario: 08:00 a 13:00 y de 14:30 a 17:30 hrs. INCLUYE: Información estratégica, material de trabajo, reconocimiento con valor oficial, coffee break y la exposición de un prestigiado consultor. FORMA DE INSCRIPCIÓN: 1.- Llenar debidamente la solicitud de inscripción. 2.- Cheque a nombre de: Quality Training Corporation, S.C. 3.- Depósito en Banamex Cuenta : 6680083 Sucursal 082 Centro Financiero Paseo 4.- Enviar por fax la ficha de su depósito sellada. 5.- Debido al cupo limitado, únicamente se garantizarán las inscripciones en el orden en que efectuaron su pago. INVERSIÓN: $ 4,690 mas IVA PRONTO PAGO: $ 4,200 mas IVA (antes del 25 de julio de 2002) INFORMES E INSCRIPCIONES: (993) 314 - 40 85 con 10 líneas Si Usted no desea recibir mas e-mails sobre nuestros exclusivos programas de capacitación o prefiere que lo enteremos por otro medio favor de hacernos llegar sus comentarios a: villahermosa_bajas@rebackee.com If you don't want to receive our information, write us an electronic mail indicating it to: villahermosa_bajas@rebackee.com ¡¡¡ Solicite Mayor información de Nuestros Exclusivos Programas !!! Quality Training de México DIRECCIÓN DE PROYECTOS VILLAHERMOSA Conmutador 01 993 914 - 40 85 con 10 líneas villahermosa@rebackee.com www.rebackee.com","[MLB-WIRELESS] CONTRALORIA Y GERENCIA ADMINISTRATIVA http://www.rebackee.com/cursos2/contraloria.htm Untitled Document Quality Training de México , lo invita al extraordinario seminario que tendrá lugar en VILLAHERMOSA , TABASCO , los días 01 y 02 de AGOSTO de 2002 Este es un seminario sobre los más efectivos conceptos y maneras concretas para mejorar la función de Contraloría y Gerencia Administrativa.....¿ Que medidas debe tomar.... para enfrentar la Falta de Liquidez, Reducción de Ventas, Aumento en los Costos, conflictos Laborales....¿ Cómo anticiparse a un colapso en la empresa ?. ¡¡ NO ESPERE A QUE SEA DEMASIADO TARDE !! Se discutirá ampliamente sobre la situación actual de las empresas en épocas de crisis, ¿que están haciendo para salir adelante?. Así como estrategias contables actuales, pronósticos de presupuestos, modelos ABC y otras alternativas de flujo de información; como controles y cumplimientos, información administrativa, reportes de gasto, crédito y cobranza, análisis financiero y personal. Aspectos claves dentro del programa : - Como organizar su área y hacerla altamente