Re: Gstreamer update,"Lance (lance_tt@bellsouth.net) wrote*: > >I really liked Ximian (back then, Helix ?) at first but, to me, Red >Hat's GNOME, released with 7.3 seems much more pretty and up-to-date. >Could this be because of inclusion of gtk2 in RH 7.3? Not many apps actually use gtk2 yet. If they do, it's obvious because it is a different tool kit. With gnomehide, I ported a lot of gtk1.2 themes to gtk2, because they are rarely compatible. Those themes are on dudex.net/rpms/ but it does not matter unless you have gnome2. In gnomehide, the apps that actually use gtk2 are Nautilus, gedit, some of the ""utility"" apps, like dictionary, calcultor, the settings applets, and of course the gnome panels and menus. -- That's ""angle"" as in geometry. _______________________________________________ RPM-List mailing list <RPM-List@freshrpms.net> http://lists.freshrpms.net/mailman/listinfo/rpm-list","Re: Gstreamer update Lance (lance_tt@bellsouth.net) wrote*: > >I really liked Ximian (back then, Helix ?) at first but, to me, Red >Hat's GNOME, released with 7.3 seems much more pretty and up-to-date. >Could this be because of inclusion of gtk2 in RH 7.3? Not many apps actually use gtk2 yet. If they do, it's obvious because it is a different tool kit. With gnomehide, I ported a lot of gtk1.2 themes to gtk2, because they are rarely compatible. Those themes are on dudex.net/rpms/ but it does not matter unless you have gnome2. In gnomehide, the apps that actually use gtk2 are Nautilus, gedit, some of the ""utility"" apps, like dictionary, calcultor, the settings applets, and of course the gnome panels and menus. -- That's ""angle"" as in geometry. _______________________________________________ RPM-List mailing list <RPM-List@freshrpms.net> http://lists.freshrpms.net/mailman/listinfo/rpm-list",0,20030228_easy_ham_2.tar.bz2,easy_ham_2/01170.fb25e6eca43ff17e87fa2ff0b39575ca,fbafbeec01f4b1b751bf3753ffc825bccb0af9ecd76b760bd0e971f7c761e921
