Re: Insert signature,"In a message dated: Thu, 22 Aug 2002 13:53:55 CDT Ulises Ponce said: >Thanks Paul, >That is the way I am doing right now, but I would like to NOT use the mouse >for such things. Any other clue? The best I can think of is to figure out what the command being issued by exmh is that selects and inserts the sig and bind that to a key sequence. That shouldn't be *too* difficult, it's just a matter of figuring out the tcl (something my perl-based brain isn't excited about :) -- Seeya, Paul -- It may look like I'm just sitting here doing nothing, but I'm really actively waiting for all my problems to go away. If you're not having fun, you're not doing it right! _______________________________________________ Exmh-users mailing list Exmh-users@redhat.com https://listman.redhat.com/mailman/listinfo/exmh-users","Re: Insert signature In a message dated: Thu, 22 Aug 2002 13:53:55 CDT Ulises Ponce said: >Thanks Paul, >That is the way I am doing right now, but I would like to NOT use the mouse >for such things. Any other clue? The best I can think of is to figure out what the command being issued by exmh is that selects and inserts the sig and bind that to a key sequence. That shouldn't be *too* difficult, it's just a matter of figuring out the tcl (something my perl-based brain isn't excited about :) -- Seeya, Paul -- It may look like I'm just sitting here doing nothing, but I'm really actively waiting for all my problems to go away. If you're not having fun, you're not doing it right! _______________________________________________ Exmh-users mailing list Exmh-users@redhat.com https://listman.redhat.com/mailman/listinfo/exmh-users",0,20030228_easy_ham.tar.bz2,easy_ham/01167.6c1a9d12bb40059b2b3aba3d1c5c0f3c,b3ce45eeaa7522c1ad44f2c0044463c99762538b79c25947552e8d8ca815b28a
