Re: [fwd: error exmh 2.5 07/13/2001 ],"F> From: kchrist@lsil.com > Date: Wed, 24 Jul 2002 15:41:04 -0600 > > I think you are referring to a problem I noticed last October (see > attached email). If I remember correctly, the binding for SeditBeautify > is being applied outside of the sedit window and that results in the > behavior observed. > > Subject: SeditBeautify bug > Date: Tue, 02 Oct 2001 15:00:16 -0600 (16:00 CDT) > From: kchrist@lsil.com > > It appears that the binding for SeditBeautify applies to > more than just the sedit window. Since SeditBeautify assumes > we are in a sedit window the routine fails. (Try typing > ctrl-l over the main window to see what I mean). > > The quick fix for this is to make the ^l more restrictive. However, I'd > suggest keeping things the way the are and extending ^l to be a > highlight toggle. If the window is currently highlighted (sedit or msg) > re-display without highlighting and vice versa. > > While I can hack tcl, hacking tk is another story. Translation: I can't > fix this bug myself. Any volunteers? That's clearly the same bug. I don't think I can fix it either...I certainly can't while my copy of Brent's book is across town. I do understand parts of tk fairly well, but the event handlers give me a headache. Chris -- Chris Garrigues http://www.DeepEddy.Com/~cwg/ virCIO http://www.virCIO.Com 716 Congress, Suite 200 Austin, TX 78701 +1 512 374 0500 World War III: The Wrong-Doers Vs. the Evil-Doers.","Re: [fwd: error exmh 2.5 07/13/2001 ] F> From: kchrist@lsil.com > Date: Wed, 24 Jul 2002 15:41:04 -0600 > > I think you are referring to a problem I noticed last October (see > attached email). If I remember correctly, the binding for SeditBeautify > is being applied outside of the sedit window and that results in the > behavior observed. > > Subject: SeditBeautify bug > Date: Tue, 02 Oct 2001 15:00:16 -0600 (16:00 CDT) > From: kchrist@lsil.com > > It appears that the binding for SeditBeautify applies to > more than just the sedit window. Since SeditBeautify assumes > we are in a sedit window the routine fails. (Try typing > ctrl-l over the main window to see what I mean). > > The quick fix for this is to make the ^l more restrictive. However, I'd > suggest keeping things the way the are and extending ^l to be a > highlight toggle. If the window is currently highlighted (sedit or msg) > re-display without highlighting and vice versa. > > While I can hack tcl, hacking tk is another story. Translation: I can't > fix this bug myself. Any volunteers? That's clearly the same bug. I don't think I can fix it either...I certainly can't while my copy of Brent's book is across town. I do understand parts of tk fairly well, but the event handlers give me a headache. Chris -- Chris Garrigues http://www.DeepEddy.Com/~cwg/ virCIO http://www.virCIO.Com 716 Congress, Suite 200 Austin, TX 78701 +1 512 374 0500 World War III: The Wrong-Doers Vs. the Evil-Doers.",0,20030228_easy_ham_2.tar.bz2,easy_ham_2/00722.7f846f5a56c251c9c49e7bd756df45d4,525aabd10ea1c1b18511cd88b86d3d90b4b3a9b72c5c0924304b2b39871e4c88
