his box) b) You must cause any work that you distribute or publish, that in whole or in part contains or is derived from the Program or any part thereof, to be licensed as a whole at no charge to all third parties under the terms of this License. Your PHP scripts do not contain, nor are they derived from, PHP, in whole or in part. > I know this is not strictly a 'Linux' issue but any help would be appreciated Microsoft has very much made this a Linux issue - it has attempted to imply that any company using GPL software must make everything it owns public and it must be true - that nice man from Microsoft wouldn't lie, would he ? Niall -- Irish Linux Users' Group: ilug@linux.ie http://www.linux.ie/mailman/listinfo/ilug for (un)subscription information. List maintainer: listmaster@linux.ie",0,20030228_easy_ham_2.tar.bz2,easy_ham_2/00115.c2fdffd60ddc035e3ac642f69301715f,6e63dc0a926148afa1be74dd3e839032ed562cd656307964f414560e0824e2f7
